 PiJev builds on [Pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) and integrates [TypeSafe's Jev](https://typesafe.ai/blog/introducing-system-one-models-and-jev), directly or through [Vercel AI Gateway](https://vercel.com/changelog/typesafe-ai-jev-now-available-on-ai-gateway). PiJev is an independent project.
 
 MIT licensed. Dependencies retain their own licenses; see [third-party notices](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
+
+### Decision ownership
+
+Decision metadata records the actual Pi session ID and an opaque `turnId` for
+the consumed user message. Steering and follow-up messages receive a distinct
+identity when Pi consumes them; repeated evaluations and cache hits for one
+message retain its identity. Ownership is captured before asynchronous work, so
+a cancelled decision stays attributed to the message and session that began it.
+`turnId` is a persisted user-entry ID, not the number of model loops. Journals
+continue to omit prompts, source text and credentials; old rows without these
+fields remain readable. `assist`, `observe` and `off` retain their prior behavior.
